  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRR awareness and preparedness in marginalised communities living in urban areas of Khulna city</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will support approximately 4,600 people living in marginalised slum areas of Khulna city in south-west Bangladesh to have better awareness and increased preparedness to face future natural and manmade disasters. This project will integrate tried and tested urban DRR initiatives into DSK&apos;s on going WASH programme in Khulna city. This allows DSK to replicate an urban DRR approach which is currently being implemented in Dhaka as well as building on a strong relationship which DSK has built with Khulna city corporation and urban marginalised communities.

This project will work to achieve four key outcomes; increased awareness and capacity of relevant stakeholders in Khulna city to manage urban hazards, increased disaster preparedness of urban schools in Khulna, activating and strengthening community based organisations to better prepare and respond to a variety of hazards as well as contributing to the government risk and action plans. Urban DRR will be integrated into the existing WASH programme which will ensure sanitation and WASH facilities are specifically considered as part of the urban DRR plans.</narrative>
  </description>
